I checked the finding myself and it holds. Only the line numbers are slightly off.

1) The Lean evidence. In /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-guygouri-Devlab-ernlang-ern/c986905c-e900-4fd9-bebc-4a3ce7ebb180/scratchpad/ref/recheck4/refute/ds4-3/P.lean I rebuilt d17 := ⟨releaseEff d11.kern 4, d11.stacks, d11.fresh⟩. The build was up to date (`lake build --no-build Ern.Lib.DataStack`), and `lake env lean` compiled the file with no errors. Theorem d17_facts proves:
- DReach K0 wst d17;
- d17.stacks[0]? = some st9;
- LiveMark 0 st9 m0;
- ¬ d17.kern.Active st9.internal;
- MetaRight d17.kern st9.entry, which still holds, so in d17 only the liveness conjunct of AdminRight fails;
- no active authority derived from internal covers a cell of above st9 m0;
- ¬ AdminRight;
- RewindStep K0 0 m0 d17 .reject, through the .static constructor.

Theorem d17_only_reject proves that reject is the only outcome. Both theorems print axioms [propext, Quot.sound]. I also checked that in d16, the DS-R12 witness, `Active st9.internal` holds and only MetaRight fails. So `reading_rewind_right` exercises the MetaRight conjunct alone.

2) The records. DS-v1 (brief.md obligation 6) says "the stack keeps the ordered list of live marks; rewind m fails on a dead or foreign mark". It never mentions a dead stack. §46 (spec line 560) says "The arena is live if internal is active", and the model's AdminRight docstring says "the stack is live (internal is active)". So the model does have a notion of a dead stack, and reading DS-v1's "dead mark" to include the marks of a dead stack is a plausible reading. On d17 that reading gives `fail` (under the DS-R2 order), against the model's `reject` and the DS-R12 alternative's `ok`. I grepped readings/datastack.md for dead/live/active wording:
- DS-R2 covers only the order of fail against §36;
- DS-R3 fixes "live" as `m.stack = j ∧ m ∈ st.marks`, and its only recorded alternative is about the stack-identity check;
- DS-R12 justifies §36 only through "MetaRight requires Modify exercisable on the stack value". It does say "rejects without AdminRight", which covers reject against ok.

No entry records the `fail` reading for a mark of a dead stack, and neither does map/libs.md (A17, C2, C3, P8). The record itself already lists analogy-based alternatives of this kind: DS-R5 takes `fail` "by analogy with DS-v1 'rewind m fails on a dead or foreign mark'". The policy requires both readings to be recorded with an example, so this is missing coverage, as the finding claims.

3) Minor imprecision only. AdminRight is at DataStack.lean:108, not 110; line 110 is its Decidable instance. DS-R12 occupies datastack.md:103-115.

I did not check the HandlePool annex for an analogous dead-pool outcome; it is not needed to confirm this finding.

